Inspect this program and report the printed value:
const arr = [1, 3500, 3];
console.log(arr.find(x => x > 100));
From this trace, select the two expressions that equal the value printed above.

Review the snippet and follow its execution:
const arr = [1, 2, 3501];
console.log(arr.some(x => x > 100));
From this trace, what boolean is printed?

In a representative snippet review, a developer inspects the code. This short script is part of a small Node utility:
const obj = null;
console.log(obj?.value ?? 3502);
In this run, explain what this code prints and why that value follows from the language rules.

In a representative snippet review, a reviewer runs the following code. The snippet below is executed in a browser console:
try {
  console.log(value);
  let value = 3503;
} catch (e) {
